The correct answer is '**has covered**'.



***__Key Points__**

__

• The sentence requires the present perfect tense to indicate an action that occurred at an indefinite time in the past and is relevant to the present.

• "**Has covered**" indicates that Hyojeong has travelled around twenty-five countries up to the present moment.

• "**Will have covered**" is incorrect because it refers to a future action that will be completed at some point.

• "**Had been covered**" is incorrect because it suggests a past perfect continuous tense, which is not suitable for the context.

• "**Was covered**" is incorrect because it indicates a simple past passive voice, which does not fit the context.

Therefore, the correct answer is '**Option 2**'.



Complete Passage: Hyojeong, a twenty-five-year-old South Korean Youtuber *has been travelling*__ since the age of 16. She **__has covered __***around twenty-five countries so far. ***___________***India was high on her wish list. She is currently soaking in the energy of Mumbai and planning to ***_________***more of this beautiful city. Unfortunately, her experience of the city turned sour recently. She was filming on the streets of Mumbai and two men tried to hug and kiss her, which was captured in her video. The video ***_________***viral and the Mumbai police swung into action.



